The cover assumes that nothing clobbers the flag between its production and transfer; a real backend must preserve that dependency through scheduling. The cost is optimal for the normalized subject and these additive weights, not over all equivalent subjects. A different machine grammar might describe a fused zero-test tile for an exclusive-or with a literal specifically on the left; always swapping that literal right would hide the tile. Test normalization for semantic preservation and termination, and test covering for completeness and cost on the shapes the normalizer actually supplies.
